  ],
  "details": "<p class=\" \">The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: T\u00e9ramo</p>\r\n<p class=\" \">In 268 B.C., a\u00a0<em>conciliabulum\u00a0civium\u00a0Romanorum</em>\u00a0was established and the Praetutii received the\u00a0<em>civitas\u00a0optimo\u00a0iure</em>.\u00a0The site became a\u00a0<em>municipium</em>\u00a0and, soon after, a\u00a0<em>colonia</em>\u00a0following the Social War.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Originally a settlement of the Praetuttii located at the confluence of the rivers Tordino and Vezzola (modern Teramo).",
